# .ipv event stream: strokes, fills, points — RE notes

Companion to [IPV_FORMAT.md](https://github.com/GGgoBRO/Ibis-.ipv-editor/blob/main/IPV_FORMAT.md)
(container, RPNG, footer). That spec covers the document *state*; this one covers the
*event stream*. Container framing was reverse-engineered independently and matches byte-for-byte.

**Legend:** ✅ round-trip verified (parse → encode is byte-identical after a JSON pass) ·
🟡 working hypothesis · ❓ unknown.
All numbers **big-endian**. Times are `f64` unix seconds. Record type ids below are
`u32 = kind<<24 | type<<8 | sub`, i.e. `(2,3)` = `0x02000300`.

**Tested on:** ibisPaint X `<13.X.X>` (Android), the author's own files.

## Stroke envelope `(2,3)` = 0x02000300 — structure ✅

| offset | type | field | status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | f64 | ts_start | ✅ |
| 8 | f64 | ts_end | ✅ |
| 16 | u32 | tool_mode | 🟡 name |
| 20 | u32 | brush_shape | 🟡 name |
| 24 | u32 | tool_category (e.g. 0x7000) | 🟡 name |
| 28 | u32 | color, bytes read as RRGGBBAA | 🟡 byte order |
| 32 | u32 | target layer id | ✅ matches layer ids |
| 36 | u32 | point count n | ✅ |

Then `n × point subframes (2,3,sub1)`, then the brush tail (below).

## Point `(2,3,sub1)` = 0x02000301

Payload: `f64 t, f32 x, f32 y` (canvas pixels) ✅.
Payload length (`sl`) is **16 or 20+** — both observed; all points of one stroke share `sl` ✅.
With `sl ≥ 20` the first extra `f32` behaves like **pressure** (0..1) 🟡.
Note: the companion spec says "No pressure is stored" — possibly version/stylus dependent.
Confirmation across app versions is welcome.

## Brush tail

Nested records ✅ framing: `(1,2,sub2)` brush parameters (292/305 bytes observed)
+ `(2,3,sub3)` (~30 bytes). Semantics mostly 🟡/❓.
Brush **size** candidates (both exposed as experimental hints by the dumper):
- `f32` at **+12** of the brush record 🟡 (per companion spec);
- last `f32` of the whole tail — **likely wrong**: it lands inside the `(2,3,sub3)` record.

## Bucket fill `(2,4)` = 0x02000400 — structure ✅

```
f64 ts_start | f64 ts_end | u32 n1 | n1 × point
u32 color (RRGGBBAA 🟡) | u32 n2 | n2 × point
rest: +4 f32 tolerance 🟡; later a repeat of ts_end followed by u32 tag 🟡
      (tag matched a stroke layer id in most observed fills)
```

Seed points are the tap locations. `n2` list purpose ❓ (same point repeated in samples).

## Observed, not yet decoded ❓

`(2,8)` selection lasso · `(2,9)` fx/filter · `(2,10)` ruler · `(2,12)` + `(2,12,3)` liquify.
The dumper preserves them byte-exact as `raw`.

## Method

Every ✅ above means: parsed fields re-encode to the exact original bytes *after* a JSON
round-trip (this catches NaN-bit and float-precision traps). Semantic names may still be 🟡.
Unknown records are never guessed — they are stored verbatim, so `dump → build` is always lossless.

## Test files that would settle the unknowns

Same canvas, one change per file: one finger stroke vs one stylus stroke (pressure);
one stroke with brush size changed (size offset); one fill with tolerance changed;
one fill on a named layer (tag).
